{"title":"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Smart_algebra_to_make_2_less_annoying)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Smart algebra to make 2 less annoying)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Alternate_Solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Alternate Solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inscribe\" title=\"Inscribe\">inscribed</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral\" title=\"Quadrilateral\">quadrilateral</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tangent\" title=\"Tangent\">tangent</a> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b937338f621cbf7cd088b106e00f8c63c85de7d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aa85963fb9c2a92405d23d3a31f1f3524f97a1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB=26$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9cda842f34661bc467363bdfdf66bab854f2d71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CQ=37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf836434104c8c0f3f651e9b8e870c89f0dd90e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QD=23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />, find the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_square\" title=\"Perfect square\">square</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a> of the circle.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Center\" title=\"Center\">center</a> of the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. By drawing the lines from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> tangent to the sides and from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the vertices of the quadrilateral, four pairs of congruent <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangles</a> are formed.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/e/1fefd39cc7109b9bda2fa7719a01af5349f98d9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{AOP}+\\angle{POB}+\\angle{COQ}+\\angle{QOD}=180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"341\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/64451310b87285c066a338d253610256c66f25d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\arctan(\\tfrac{19}{r})+\\arctan(\\tfrac{26}{r}))+(\\arctan(\\tfrac{37}{r})+\\arctan(\\tfrac{23}{r}))=180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"473\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Take the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75b04387daddfdad2ef55b5a9dfec552ea41db50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan$\" width=\"26\" height=\"11\" /> of both sides and use the identity for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef10d4623066d7490b24351c8f9bb597e107c04f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(A+B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10d199ea13199b92aa7ee186b88f17c3facdac3f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan(\\arctan(\\tfrac{19}{r})+\\arctan(\\tfrac{26}{r}))+\\tan(\\arctan(\\tfrac{37}{r})+\\arctan(\\tfrac{23}{r}))=n\\cdot0=0.\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Use the identity for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef10d4623066d7490b24351c8f9bb597e107c04f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(A+B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> again to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d29e7ed99258e5a4ffe3dce264d0d35eb5d2362.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\tfrac{45}{r}}{1-19\\cdot\\tfrac{26}{r^2}}+\\frac{\\tfrac{60}{r}}{1-37\\cdot\\tfrac{23}{r^2}}=0.\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Solving gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d6fd771ec1c510aea7b84daebde9a7b23ae0b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2=\\boxed{647}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Note: the equation may seem nasty at first, but once you cancel the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />s and other factors, you are just left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e2221c84f16a3f75ae07e5023384cc40d9c05357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />. That gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2afd65a3c1775ecfae081e22652ba8d0b38c95c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$647$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> quite easily.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Just use the area formula for tangential quadrilaterals. The numbers are really big. A terrible problem to work on (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d02bb2275100261109b043261e702124460a83e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are the tangent lengths, not the side lengths).\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1ea5edc88f82cfc369d50547923150dfa497d4d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A = \\sqrt{(a+b+c+d)(abc+bcd+cda+dab)} = 105\\sqrt{647}\\]\" width=\"450\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/a/38ac78828e479d20ecb4f580c756afe94d80a5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2=\\frac{A^2}{(a+b+c+d)^2} = \\boxed{647}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"232\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Smart_algebra_to_make_2_less_annoying.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Smart_algebra_to_make_2_less_annoying)\">Solution 3 (Smart algebra to make 2 less annoying)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Smart algebra to make 2 less annoying)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the formulas established in solution 2, one notices:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58d0177dced99eb8bf005d39fa57607f7a7f1a02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2=\\frac{A^2}{(a+b+c+d)^2}\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"44\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/6/d96fe4f12c44152b152ac43bbf722e3d562beaf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2=\\frac{(a+b+c+d)(abc+bcd+cda+abd) }{(a+b+c+d)^2}\\]\" width=\"343\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/9/bb9bb28e5952a3a9f2a1d47418a8057875c33bf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2=\\frac{abc+bcd+acd+abd}{a+b+c+d}\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/9/9c9171f3e7c73b6c8155565038345618f8c788a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2=\\boxed{647}\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>which is nowhere near as hard of a calculation. In fact, this is basically the same exact calculation done at the end of solution 1, just with less opportunity to cancel coefficients beforehand.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Alternate_Solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Alternate_Solution_2)\">Solution 4 (Alternate Solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Alternate Solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of a tangential quadrilateral using side and tangential lengths is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/9/ba9494227e300b689bcaa7b52e7195ff7f328f61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K = \\sqrt{(abcd) - (eg-fh)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"215\" height=\"35\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are the side lengths, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, the tangential lengths. Then, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/330147780082bca29c5064dc379d735443917323.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f55ca08f4837e8bcd9a9f9d5339d87b28c601ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f= 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/a/f5a135f3a846cddcdad64cc8ebe89e155d73dbce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf154c42cb8eb4d8b5c57f59e36cf6cb433d68b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, the lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5073431893e72faf624b0ff92249636a19500f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed19c4f1de0a66d3f79d5a7872fd1e431e1fb61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/b/eabd4024242f613201ee620cc54f51ae9df0117d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad28e3c81f470a7baea3b13b1ecdcd17dc531a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8fa4a6b2b49068304c516b6c1ce9148cae814e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K = \\sqrt{7144200 - 11025} = \\sqrt{7133175} = 105\\sqrt{647}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"386\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>Then, use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda6dd435464c5a60973d095cba881347682d011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K = rs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac750781287efc83dd1a0f6d4f9c18616359cc34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = \\frac{a+b+c+d}{2} = \\frac{210}{2} = 105$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"247\" height=\"39\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9cbb217ba95f38b7301f360f7e214d6b543110e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{647}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />, squared is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f79f564b6a5b63b3222f3b578199cca04985bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{647}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II\" title=\"2000 AIME II\">2000 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2000\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AIME II Problems/P